 "identity_claim": "Single-request identity holds: both depth-3 servers matched each other and the same-configuration MTP0 oracle on all 12 complete token arrays. Concurrency identity does not hold to the top of the ladder on two cards: without speculation the route is exact through 32 users in both passes and 62/64 then 64/64 at 64 users; with depth 3 it is exact through 16 users, 30/32 and 28/32 at 32, and 60/64 then 59/64 at 64. The one-card 9B on this same kernel is exact at every rung through 64 in both passes, so the loss appears when a second card joins.",
 "notes": "Canaries passed on every server; cached_tokens 0 on every request. The two depth-3 servers measured 240.615 and 227.533 tok/s, a 5.8% spread, against 0.13% between the two one-card servers of the same lane: two-card speculative decode is markedly noisier here, so its center is reported with that spread stated."
